Falsifies `file_system_contract::proofs::the_attribute_list_walk_ends`.

The defect: `extended_attribute::list::iter` advances by the name alone and skips the length byte, so records overlap.

Expected to fail: `assert!(consumed <= length)`, and the unwinding assertion of the walk's loop.

diff --git a/src/extended_attribute.rs b/src/extended_attribute.rs
--- a/src/extended_attribute.rs
+++ b/src/extended_attribute.rs
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@
                 return None;
             }
             let name = self.buf.get(self.at + 1..self.at + 1 + len)?;
-            self.at += record_len(len);
+            self.at += len;
             Some(name)
         }
     }
